# Approved request
Implement Work parallel execution with P1-P5 admission, natural-language policy changes, review/rework, cleanup verification, Claude-first/Codex adapter boundary; deploy to nightly. SSE configuration accepts an external idle-discovery instruction. Test default: search Walkie unresolved items by priority then latest creation time. Approval/block waits must include independent-item pickup guidance without approving blocked work.

# Latest deletion rule
Worktrees may be removed only after their HEAD is verified on a remote ref OR the user explicitly approved deletion of that exact target. Dirty/active/unowned targets remain blocked regardless. No force removal, no automatic branch deletion.

# Isolation
Base: remote nightly 4758efb. Dedicated feature/work-parallel-20261103 worktree. Root checkout has unrelated statusline changes and remains untouched. No live router restart or live test sweep.

# Verification so far
24 focused unittest tests passed across discovery policy, external SSE settings and existing concurrent Work mod gates (including two new approval/block discovery scenarios). Real local Git worktree cleanup: five cases passed, including pushed, unpushed, explicit approval and dirty retention. Parallel engine agent reported 35 tests; parent rerun after aligning Korean default: 34 pass, one outdated default-text assertion failed and corrected, rerun pending.

# Not yet verified
Actual Claude fork execution/host identity, full coordinator integration, real menu actions and screenshots, nightly publication. No deployment claim yet.

